{
  "$comment": "DDD bridge for GitHub Primer (@primer/primitives). Tiers follow elements/d-d-d/design-system/bridge/contract.json. Primer's color tokens only exist per theme (light.css, dark.css), so named DDD colors take the light theme's value as a constant (fromMode), the way the Spectrum bridge does; theme chrome uses the functional tokens, which follow light and dark. Primer's size tokens are rem, and HAX's root font size is 20px, not 16px, so radii, control heights and density are written as px values with the upstream token named in the note. Kept as DDD on purpose: black font weight (Primer's heaviest is semibold), state opacities (Primer uses hover colors), border widths and heading/body sizes (Primer body is 14px, below the 16px floor). Primer's spacing steps (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32px) sit on DDD's 4px grid, so the theme chrome uses DDD spacing tokens.",
